Subject: [PATCH 1245/3799] soh: rename func_800C09D8 -> Play_CheckCameraActive

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: meant to report whether the camera at a given id still matches a uid and is active, returning 2 for inactive and 1 for active. Nothing calls it, and its first branch returns 0 whenever the camera is non-NULL, which makes every later branch unreachable and would dereference NULL if it were ever taken -- so the name describes the evident intent, not the behaviour.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_play.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/z_play.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_play.c b/soh/src/code/z_play.c
index 9112d7000..03c02e211 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_play.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_play.c
@@ -2039,7 +2039,8 @@ s16 Play_CameraGetUID(PlayState* play, s16 camId) {
     }
 }
 
-s16 func_800C09D8(PlayState* play, s16 camId, s16 arg2) {
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was func_800C09D8: meant to report whether the camera at a given id still matches a uid and is active, returning 2 for inactive and 1 for active. Nothing calls it, and its first branch returns 0 whenever the camera is non-NULL, which makes every later branch unreachable and would dereference NULL if it were ever taken -- so the name describes the evident intent, not the behaviour.
+s16 Play_CheckCameraActive(PlayState* play, s16 camId, s16 arg2) {
     Camera* camera = play->cameraPtrs[camId];
 
     if (camera != NULL) {
